    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, led by the dynamic trio of **Gunnar Henderson** (68.57), **Brady House** (63.18), and **Jackson Merrill** (60.00). **Gunnar Henderson** remains our most reliable anchor; despite facing an arm like Meyer with a 3.69 xERA, his leadoff spot and favorable platoon split (R vs R) push his efficiency score well into the strong category. **Brady House** stands out as an intriguing play at 63.18, benefiting significantly from a favorable matchup against Woods Richardson (4.85 xERA); the combination of his power profile and a +9% boost from his platoon advantage makes him a cornerstone for today\u2019s production. While we are tracking the lineup status for **Jackson Merrill**, his high-volume leadoff role compensates for the slight handicap of facing a lefty in Liberatore, ensuring he remains a priority start.\n\nThe bench decision for **Coby Mayo** (37.37) was the most difficult pivot, as he narrowly missed the 40.0 efficiency floor required for inclusion. While his raw projections were competitive, the combination of a low batting order (#8) and the difficult matchup against Meyer ultimately lowered his score below the acceptable threshold. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Nasim Nunez**, whose score of 59.75 is largely driven by his elite sprint speed and a soft matchup against Woods Richardson. Despite hitting in the nine-hole, his stolen base potential remains the primary engine for his inclusion in our 5x5 Roto strategy. We continue to monitor the statuses of **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, though they are unavailable today due to schedule gaps or injury, leaving us to rely on our secondary depth to maintain our category standings.",
